L001188	\section{Appendix C: The Origin of Universal Time Evolution}\label{sec:apptime}
L001189	
L001190	In this appendix, we extend our analysis beyond the Gaussian Unitary Ensemble (GUE) in random matrix theory, generalizing previous conclusions about the time evolution of holographic and quantum complexity to broader classes of quantum chaotic systems. We begin with the codimension-one observables. Using the unscaled density of states $\rho(E)$, the generating function of complexity is defined as
L001191	\begin{equation}\label{eq:spectraltwopoint02}
L001192	 \langle e^{-\alpha \mC} \rangle \equiv  \langle \text{TFD}(t)|\, \widehat{e^{-\alpha \mC }} \, |\text{TFD}(t) \rangle  = \frac{1}{Z} \int dE_idE_j \,e^{-iE_{ij}t}  \times \overline{\langle  \rho(E_i) \rho(E_j) \rangle }  \times  \langle E_i | \widehat{e^{-\alpha \mC }}| E_j \rangle  \,.
L001193	\end{equation}
L001194	The key observation is that, by construction, all time dependence in the spectral representation arises solely from the phase factor $e^{-i E_{ij} t}$. This originates from the fact that the boundary time as a boundary condition for the state preparation determines the Lorentzian time evolution of TFD state $| \text{TFD}(t) \rangle$.
